---
// chefkiss: the mod's page on the site, where its tile leads (site.md §9). Copy verbatim: the line from the repository's
// About, the paragraphs, the install lines and the video's description from its README, the sign-off from /glass. Laid
// out as the wall (site.css): the line at Display, the README's edited recording of a real session under it as a print
// on the wall, captions in the caption half.
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";

const REPO = "https://github.com/phileeppov/chefkiss";
const CLIP =
  "An edited recording of a real Claude Code session (camera, captions and speed-ups added): 💩 on a line from a LinkedIn post about coffee, and Claude replies 'got it: avoid stock LinkedIn-style hooks and tidy moral twists'; then 🎯 on a git tip and 🤌 on a coffee shop tagline, each with its own one-line reply.";
---

<Site
  passage
  title="chefkiss"
  description="A 💩 button for AI slop. Claude takes the hint. Every answer in Claude Code gets three buttons: 🤌 for how it's said, 🎯 for what it says, 💩 for AI slop."
  image="/chefkiss-og.png"
  imageSize={[1280, 640]}
>
  <main class="wall chefkiss">
    <section class="intro grid">
      <h1 class="label">CHEFKISS</h1>
      <p class="statement"><span class="ph"><span>A 💩 button</span> <span>for&nbsp;AI&nbsp;slop.</span> <span>Claude&nbsp;takes the&nbsp;hint.</span></span></p>
      <!-- The recording, not a drawing: an animation reads as a mock-up, a real session as proof. It plays while a
           quarter of it is in view; with reduced motion, only its first frame. -->
      <figure class="clip">
        <video src="/media/chefkiss-2026.mp4" poster="/media/chefkiss-2026.jpg" width="1600" height="900" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label={CLIP}></video>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="part grid" aria-labelledby="what-label">
      <h2 class="label" id="what-label">WHAT IT DOES</h2>
      <div class="cap">
        <p>Every answer in Claude Code gets three buttons: 🤌 for how it's said, 🎯 for what it says, 💩 for AI slop. Select a sentence first to react to that part only (in the desktop app). Claude replies to each click with a one-line takeaway, and new sessions start with your latest ones, 15 at most, in every&nbsp;project.</p>
        <p>Animated buttons in the desktop app, plain emoji in the&nbsp;terminal.</p>
        <p>After a few reactions, the <code>/chefkiss</code> pane can sum you up: one line about you, up to five on how you like your answers. Cross out what it got wrong and post the rest. Forget all erases lessons, the summary, and&nbsp;reactions.</p>
        <p>Why not a line in CLAUDE.md? You click in the moment instead of editing a file, you can react to a single sentence, and Claude's reply shows right away whether it&nbsp;understood.</p>
        <p>Lessons are stored on your machine, and the mod doesn't save Claude's answers. There's no chefkiss&nbsp;server.</p>
        <p>Each click costs one Sonnet call on your Claude Code account, about&nbsp;500&nbsp;tokens. Sum up is one more call, only when you press&nbsp;it. You can turn those calls off in Settings; details in <a class="link" href={`${REPO}#what-gets-sent-where`} data-gem>what&nbsp;gets&nbsp;sent&nbsp;where</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="part grid" aria-labelledby="install-label">
      <h2 class="label" id="install-label">INSTALL</h2>
      <div class="cap">
        <p>At the prompt of a Claude Code terminal session:</p>
        <!-- The command as it is typed, in two halves that wrap only at their spaces (never after the "--"); on a phone
             word by word. The key copies its text whole, however it wraps. -->
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <div class="cmd"><code><span class="g"><span>/plugin</span> <span>install</span> <span>chefkiss</span></span> <span class="g"><span>--marketplace</span> <span>phileeppov/chefkiss</span></span></code><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy data-gem-off>Copy</button></div>
        <p>In the desktop app, where <code>/plugin</code> does not run: click + next to the prompt box, then Plugins, Add marketplace with <code>phileeppov/chefkiss</code>, then Add&nbsp;plugin.</p>
        <a class="btn" href={REPO} data-gem data-count="chefkiss:repo">Source on GitHub <span class="arw">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The sign-off of /glass: who made it, and the way to the review; under it the line the README ends on. -->
    <section class="part end grid">
      <div class="cap">
        <p>Made by Nikita Filippov ☺</p>
        <p>Product designer.<br /><a class="link" href="/review/" data-gem data-count="chefkiss:review">Send your product or idea, get a video review <span class="arw">→</span></a></p>
        <p class="meta">Not affiliated with Anthropic.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>

<script>
  import { count } from "../scripts/review-count";

  count("chefkiss:view");

  // The recording plays while a quarter of it is in view and pauses out of view; with reduced motion, only the poster.
  const video = document.querySelector<HTMLVideoElement>(".clip video");
  if (video && !matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) {
    new IntersectionObserver(
      ([e]) => {
        if (e.isIntersecting) video.play().catch(() => {});
        else video.pause();
      },
      { threshold: 0.25 },
    ).observe(video);
  }

  // Copy: the line as written, then a moment of "Copied" on the key.
  for (const key of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]")) {
    key.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const line = key.parentElement?.querySelector("code")?.textContent ?? "";
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(line);
      } catch {
        return;
      }
      count("chefkiss:copy");
      key.textContent = "Copied";
      window.setTimeout(() => (key.textContent = "Copy"), 1600);
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-bottom: 120px;
  }
  .intro .label,
  .intro .statement {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .intro .statement {
    margin-top: 72px;
  }
  /* The recording: a print on the wall over eight columns, like the shots of the cases: a small radius, a 0.5px edge. */
  .clip {
    grid-column: 1 / span 8;
    margin: 96px 0 0;
  }
  .clip video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.5px var(--hair);
  }

  /* Parts: the label under the hairline, the caption 48px under it, a long rest after. */
  .part {
    row-gap: 0;
    padding-bottom: 160px;
  }
  .part > .label {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .part > .cap {
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .cap p + p {
    margin-top: 1em;
  }
  .cap .btn {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .cap code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .meta {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .end {
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }

  /* The command: a black block, the line in monospace at body size, the key inside it on the right. A long line wraps
     at its spaces; the key copies it whole. */
  .cmd {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 16px 0;
    padding: 12px 12px 12px 20px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: var(--color-black);
    color: var(--color-off-white);
  }
  .cmd code span {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .cmd code {
    flex: 1;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  /* Its radius is the block's less the 12px between them: the same curve, one step in. */
  .copy {
    flex: none;
    min-width: 76px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-off-white) 14%, var(--color-black));
    box-shadow: inset 0 0.5px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-off-white) 16%, transparent);
    color: inherit;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 120ms ease-out;
  }
  .copy:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-off-white) 22%, var(--color-black));
  }
  .copy:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-off-white);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .clip {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .clip {
      margin-top: 56px;
    }
    .part {
      padding-bottom: 120px;
    }
    .cmd {
      padding-left: 16px;
      border-radius: 16px;
    }
    .cmd code .g {
      white-space: normal;
    }
    .copy {
      min-width: 0;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
